{
  "_createdAt": "2026-04-27T18:25:31Z",
  "_id": "wp-post-205954-en",
  "_rev": "dJ4ZpMyfIFtQ0D7lyxX9cl",
  "_type": "article",
  "_updatedAt": "2026-07-05T14:28:16Z",
  "author": {
    "_ref": "author-legacy-archive",
    "_type": "reference"
  },
  "body": [
    {
      "_key": "000000000001",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000000",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "To travel Siwa, lining up sights isn't enough."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000003",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000002",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Culture and landscape aren't separated here. Date-palm groves, salt lakes, springs, desert roads, Shali's ruins, silver jewellery, embroidery, the town's quiet. All connect inside one environment called Siwa."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000005",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "8vl4yg7hh40p",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa is an oasis in Egypt's Western Desert. Far from "
        },
        {
          "_key": "wwuhqqkhs0xy",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "oqoo0ls3skz9"
          ],
          "text": "Cairo"
        },
        {
          "_key": "hvciq4z9jc9i",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", near the Libyan border, off the Nile-valley main tourist route. So a trip this far needs reason."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "oqoo0ls3skz9",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-83284",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000007",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "9x5n594r06ty",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The reason is clear. In Siwa, another face of Egypt appears. Not pyramids-and-temples Egypt but oasis life continuing around water, Amazigh culture, a community protected by desert, and the wide landscape heading to "
        },
        {
          "_key": "1as2z6pi7rt2",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "hxqpzu0d5rw7"
          ],
          "text": "the Great Sand Sea"
        },
        {
          "_key": "t7zi510doajq",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "hxqpzu0d5rw7",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.siwa-oasis.the-great-sand-sea",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000009",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000008",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Understand the culture first"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000000a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa is an Amazigh-culture town inside Egypt."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000000c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Most residents speak Siwi. A separate language from Egyptian Arabic, in the North African Amazigh family. Arabic is widely used daily; Siwi supports this town's distinctness."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000000e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "What matters for travellers is not consuming Siwa as \"a rustic desert village.\" A living community. Market, family, religion, dress, photography, and festivals each have their own distance."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000011",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000010",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In town, avoid exposed dress. For water at springs or salt lakes, carry a cover for transit and town walking. When photographing locals, especially women and children, always seek permission. Photos without permission aren't trip records — they are invasion of someone's life."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000013",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000012",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Just these basics make the Siwa trip much better."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000015",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000014",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa House Museum and crafts"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000017",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "9t6wg0rbqyxp",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "To know Siwa culture, going first to "
        },
        {
          "_key": "w1cnembm2hpo",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "ts1sjtnezovl"
          ],
          "text": "the Siwa House Museum"
        },
        {
          "_key": "vg7xqarag6vy",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " has value."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "ts1sjtnezovl",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.siwa-oasis.siwa-house-museum",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000019",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000018",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Not a big museum. Embroidery, silver jewellery, traditional dress, furniture, and household goods give background to market items."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa silverwork and embroidery have vocabulary different from Nile-valley craft. Wedding dresses, necklaces, bracelets, and embroidery patterns held meaning beyond ornament. Tied to family, ritual, status, and festival."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Today's market lines up tourist-made pieces too. Not bad in itself. Treating old traditional craft and new souvenirs as the same thins Siwa culture. Before buying, see, ask, understand — that order fits."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Walking Shali"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000021",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000020",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The strongest presence at Siwa's centre is the ruins of Shali."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000023",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000022",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Shali was a fortified town built from kershef — salt, mud, and clay mixed. Developing from around the 13th century, it functioned as a dense living space protecting residents from outside threat and desert harshness."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000025",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000024",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Kershef suits dry climate; weak to water. In the 1926 heavy rains many buildings collapsed and residents moved to the plain. The Shali remaining now isn't a restored historic district — it is traces of a city continuing to weather."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000027",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000026",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "When walking, don't see ruins only as backdrop. Shali shows how Siwa people gathered, defended, and lived. Climb in the evening and town, palms, salt lakes, and desert appear at once. To understand Siwa's geography, one of the clearest places."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000029",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000028",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The oracle temple and ancient memory"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "What made Siwa famous in the ancient world was the Oracle of Amun."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The oracle temple at Aghurmi isn't complete in form. With Alexander the Great's 331 BC visit, Siwa was deeply carved into Mediterranean-world history."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "What Alexander asked and what the oracle exactly answered differs in sources. He treated this visit as important both politically and religiously. Siwa's oracle was not a mere provincial sacred place — a place tied to power and legitimacy."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000031",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "r1s4dk4my9fx",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Don't expect scale at the oracle temple. Not the overwhelming architecture of Karnak or "
        },
        {
          "_key": "j47v46laxgu1",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "qsbvw62frsw5"
          ],
          "text": "Abu Simbel"
        },
        {
          "_key": "ksam0wjo0hei",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ". What matters more than the remaining stone is that this place deep in the desert held meaning for ancient kings."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "qsbvw62frsw5",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-56813",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000033",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000032",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Salt lakes and springs"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000035",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000034",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa's water isn't tourism landscape. It is the reason the town exists."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000037",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000036",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Springs support date palms and olives; salt lakes are part of Siwa's landscape and environment. The Spring of Cleopatra is an accessible place to experience the springwater. The name spread through tourism; no firm evidence Cleopatra herself visited."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000039",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000038",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In salt lakes, high salinity floats the body naturally. Popular as photogenic; salt lakes are delicate. They sting on cuts and hurt eyes. After entering, have freshwater rinse ready."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Salt lakes and springs also tie to water-management issues. Beautiful tourism for visitors, locally tied to agriculture, drainage, groundwater, and salt damage. Enjoying and respecting as resource can happen together."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Going to the Great Sand Sea"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa's adventure feel comes through clearest at the Great Sand Sea."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000041",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000040",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Outside town, dunes, fossil-bearing strata, desert springs, sunset, and stars become trip centre. Half-day, full-day 4WD tours, or overnight desert plans."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000043",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000042",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Popular is the evening dune trip. Day heat drops, light softens, sand form reads. Sandboarding can combine; enjoy as play. What matters is feeling the desert's vastness and the oasis's smallness with the body."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000045",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000044",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For the desert, always go with experienced local guides. Many places have no visible road; vehicle condition, weather, sand depth, and water preparation matter. Not a place to enter only on map app."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000047",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000046",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Whether to overnight in the desert"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000049",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000048",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "With time, overnighting in the desert is a Siwa-like trip."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "At night, away from town lights, the sky grows large. Temperature drops, feeling like a completely different place from daytime dunes. Fire, simple meals, and stars combined as camp stay strongly with many travellers."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Different from comfortable hotel stays. Confirm toilets, bedding, cold, wind, sand, food, and transfer time in advance. Choosing on photos alone produces gap between expectation and reality."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Winter especially cools at night. The idea \"desert means warm\" is dangerous. Prepare layers, warm gear, and walking shoes."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000051",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000050",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Bicycle and town walking"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000053",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000052",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa town and surroundings move well on bicycle."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000055",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000054",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Shali, the Spring of Cleopatra, fields, and parts of nearby springs and salt lakes can loop by bike. Rather than point to point by car, seeing fields and palm groves along the road makes the town's sense graspable."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000057",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000056",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Avoid bike movement in hot hours. Roads with little shade; going without water is dangerous. Sand and unpaved sections ride hard in places."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000059",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000058",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For town walking, beyond the central square and market, time walking the edge of palm groves is good. Siwa, beyond sights, creates trip impression through daily rhythm."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Festivals and visiting distance"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa has the Siyaha festival as a known autumn event."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "An important event tied to local social reconciliation and unity, not staging for tourists. With timing, you may feel the town's air differs from usual; travellers should keep careful distance."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000061",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000060",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Festivals, weddings, religious events, and family gatherings aren't stages for photos. Even if guide or local permits, respect the place's meaning."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000063",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000062",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Cultural experience isn't a right to see something up close. It is awareness of being let into someone's life."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000065",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000064",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "How many nights"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000067",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000066",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Hurrying Siwa, two nights works."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000069",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000068",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Day one arrive and walk town, day two include oracle temple, Shali, salt lakes, springs, and Great Sand Sea sunset, day three depart. Slightly busy, with transfer fatigue remaining."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000006b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000006a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For Siwa-feel, three nights is realistic. Town walking, sites, salt lakes, desert, and museum split without strain. For desert overnight, photography, craft, fields, and market time, four or more nights work."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000006d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000006c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "One-night Siwa isn't recommended. Too short against transfer length."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000006f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000006e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "When to go"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000071",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000070",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Most suited for Siwa, October to April."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000073",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000072",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Day walks well; desert excursions are realistic. December to February cool at night — warm layers needed. March-April and October-November balance temperature and ease often."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000075",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000074",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Summer is very hot, sightseeing takes stamina. Limited to early morning and evening, possible; not very suited for first Siwa. People not used to heat, families with children or older travellers — choose season carefully."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000077",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000076",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Ramadan shifts food, shop times, and town rhythm. Quiet by day, lively at night. Travel works; hold margin for meal arrangement and transfer time."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000079",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000078",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Trips that fit Siwa"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000007b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000007a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa isn't a convenient destination."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000007d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "vjh03pzdrkwg",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Long transfer, limited city-style comfort, weather and road affect. On a short Egypt trip without Cairo, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "o0aswpq0r9hl",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "oefpy8v654l3"
          ],
          "text": "Giza"
        },
        {
          "_key": "kz5xralmbmnv",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "_key": "5n5i3yyknsry",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "b97n2n7sfv25"
          ],
          "text": "Luxor"
        },
        {
          "_key": "cq7u5xzt3byu",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", or "
        },
        {
          "_key": "7axlf8owrqko",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "3noyj25o0d6m"
          ],
          "text": "Aswan"
        },
        {
          "_key": "xv0wtqfovai0",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", no need to force Siwa."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "oefpy8v654l3",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58854",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "b97n2n7sfv25",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58877",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "3noyj25o0d6m",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58758",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000007f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000007e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For people wanting to see Egypt a bit deeper, Siwa has high value. Amazigh culture, oasis water, desert roads, ancient oracle, local craft, night dunes. All give understanding different from Nile-centred Egypt."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000081",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000080",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa's adventure isn't going far."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000083",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000082",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Respecting culture, not treating desert lightly, and not rushing time. With that attitude, Siwa becomes not just \"a rare place\" but a trip that changes how you see Egypt."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    }
  ],
